      "side": 0,
      "message": "I wonder if the blob shouldn\u0027t be provided to both start and finish.  An implementation that wanted to use signing would need to hold a copy of the key throughout the retrieval process in order to do the signature at the end, which could be a challenge for constrained environments.  OTOH, we don\u0027t really want to encourage signing, and I suppose this approach may encourage use of MACing instead.  On the gripping hand, the cost of passing it to both is very low -- and a HAL service for an implementation that doesn\u0027t need one or the other can just ignore it -- and there may be some case in which MACing can\u0027t be used.\n\nThoughts?",
